# Supabase CLI local state
supabase/.temp/

# Production schema dumps written by scripts/clone-schema-to-dev.ps1. This
# repository is public, and the dump reproduces every function body and RLS
# expression in production. The script redacts the webhook trigger that carries
# credentials and aborts on any JWT-shaped string, but that guard only knows the
# shapes of today's secrets, and the file is regenerated on every clone.
# Regenerate it locally with -DumpOnly whenever it is needed.
supabase/migrations/*_baseline_public.sql

# Destructive one-shot scripts that have already been executed against production.
# The safe, guarded copy lives in supabase/_archive/. If an editor ever recreates
# the original at the path below (e.g. from a stale buffer), this rule ensures it
# can never be re-tracked or committed by accident. Never delete this line.
/supabase/clear_feed_pre_launch.sql
